  "nl_text": "The rschema_0308 database is designed to manage information about customers, projects, and user accounts. The customer table stores details about each customer, including their unique customer ID, name, address, contact information, and any additional remarks. The project table contains information about each project, such as its unique project ID, name, start date, status, scale, remarks, and the project manager's user ID, which references the user table. The project_report table stores reports related to each project, including the report date, time, description, creator's user ID, and the associated project ID, which references the project table. The user table stores information about each user, including their unique user ID, name, abbreviation, password, active status, and status information. The project_customer_record table serves as a bridge between the customer and project tables, linking each customer to the projects they are associated with, and vice versa, with each record uniquely identified by a combination of the customer ID and project ID. The database enforces referential integrity through various constraints, such as the ON DELETE CASCADE rule, which automatically deletes related records in other tables when a record is deleted, ensuring data consistency across the database.",
  "gold_question": "The project management and customer relationship management system needs to implement the following functionalities. The system shall be able to manage customer information, including customer name, ID, address, contact information, and remarks. Each customer is uniquely identified by an ID. The system supports project management, recording project information including project name, associated customer, start date, status, scale, and remarks. Each project is managed by a specific project manager. The reporting system associated with projects also needs to support report management functionality, generating and recording information including report date, time, description, and creator. User management is one of the fundamental functions of the system, needing to record user name, abbreviation, password, active status, and status information, ensuring user abbreviations are unique within the system, and users can be activated or deactivated.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0308.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0308\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `remarks` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `abbreviation` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `active_status` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  `status_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project` (\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `start_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `scale` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `remarks` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `project_manager_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`project_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `project_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_manager_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project_report` (\n  `report_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `report_time` time NOT NULL,\n  `description` text NOT NULL,\n  `creator_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`report_date`, `report_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `project_report_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`creator_user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `project_report_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project_customer_record` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`, `project_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `project_customer_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `project_customer_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
